# The repo root IS the project directory now, so this only has to exclude
# generated artefacts.
#
# It previously used a whitelist rooted at $HOME (`/*` then re-admit patterns),
# because the repo had been initialised in the home directory alongside ~81GB
# of unrelated data. That was treating the symptom: the whitelist silently
# excluded every new directory, and the entire tekdromo package went uncommitted
# without any warning. Rooting the repo at the project fixes the cause.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# rendered output and screen captures
tek_out/

# derived geometry cache, keyed by a hash of the source
*.npz

# Piper voice models: 61MB of binary per voice, refetchable from
# huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices - see tools/fetch_voice.sh
voices/
